      "summaries": {
        "en": "curl is a command-line tool and library for transferring data using URL syntax, supporting over 20 protocols including HTTP, FTP, and SFTP. Its key strength lies in its simplicity and universality—one command handles diverse protocols without additional tools. Developers can embed libcurl into applications for file transfers, API testing, or automation. Use it to download files, test endpoints, or script complex data workflows.",
        "zh": "curl 是一个命令行工具和库，通过 URL 语法传输数据，支持 HTTP、FTP、SFTP 等 20 多种协议。它的核心优势在于简洁和通用——一条命令即可处理多种协议，无需额外工具。开发者可将 libcurl 嵌入应用，用于文件传输、API 测试或自动化。你可以用它下载文件、测试接口，或编写脚本实现复杂的数据处理流程。",
        "es": "curl is a command-line tool and library for transferring data using URL syntax, supporting over 20 protocols including HTTP, FTP, and SFTP. Its key strength lies in its simplicity and universality—one command handles diverse protocols without additional tools. Developers can embed libcurl into applications for file transfers, API testing, or automation. Use it to download files, test endpoints, or script complex data workflows.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "curl stands out for c, client, and curl in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "curl is a command-line tool and library for transferring data using URL syntax, supporting over 20 protocols including HTTP, FTP, and SFTP. Its key strength lies in its simplicity and universality—one command handles diverse protocols without additional tools. Developers can embed libcurl into applications for file transfers, API testing, or automation. Use it to download files, test endpoints, or script complex data workflows.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/curl/curl for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
