      "summaries": {
        "en": "CUA is an open-source infrastructure for building and evaluating computer-use agents that control desktops (macOS, Linux, Windows). It provides sandboxed environments, SDKs, and benchmarks, enabling safe training and testing of AI agents that perform GUI tasks like clicking, typing, and navigating. Technically, it uses containerization to isolate agent actions, ensuring reproducibility and safety. Developers can use CUA to prototype desktop automation agents, benchmark their performance, or integrate it into larger AI workflows.",
        "zh": "CUA 是一个开源基础设施，用于构建和评估能够控制桌面（macOS、Linux、Windows）的计算机使用智能体。它提供沙盒环境、SDK 和基准测试，使 AI 智能体能够安全地训练和测试点击、输入、导航等 GUI 任务。技术核心是通过容器化隔离智能体操作，确保可复现性和安全性。开发者可以利用 CUA 快速原型化桌面自动化智能体，在标准基准上评估其性能，或将其集成到更大的 AI 工作流中。",
        "es": "CUA is an open-source infrastructure for building and evaluating computer-use agents that control desktops (macOS, Linux, Windows). It provides sandboxed environments, SDKs, and benchmarks, enabling safe training and testing of AI agents that perform GUI tasks like clicking, typing, and navigating. Technically, it uses containerization to isolate agent actions, ensuring reproducibility and safety. Developers can use CUA to prototype desktop automation agents, benchmark their performance, or integrate it into larger AI workflows.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "cua stands out for agent, ai-agent, and apple in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "CUA is an open-source infrastructure for building and evaluating computer-use agents that control desktops (macOS, Linux, Windows). It provides sandboxed environments, SDKs, and benchmarks, enabling safe training and testing of AI agents that perform GUI tasks like clicking, typing, and navigating. Technically, it uses containerization to isolate agent actions, ensuring reproducibility and safety. Developers can use CUA to prototype desktop automation agents, benchmark their performance, or integrate it into larger AI workflows.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/trycua/cua for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
